Day 4 — AWS IAM + Security + Access Management

STAR-approach DevOps Interview Questions 

1️⃣ Your organization has multiple AWS accounts. How will you design IAM roles, groups, and permission boundaries to enforce least privilege?

2️⃣ A developer accidentally pushed an IAM access key to GitHub. What immediate and long-term actions will you take?

3️⃣ You need to implement SSO across AWS accounts using an external Identity Provider. How will you design this?

4️⃣ Your CI/CD pipeline requires temporary credentials to deploy resources. How will you implement secure role assumption?

5️⃣ An application needs cross-account access to an S3 bucket. How will you design secure cross-account IAM trust?

6️⃣ Your security team mandates MFA for all privileged operations. How will you enforce MFA and handle exceptions?

7️⃣ An IAM user has admin privileges but does not need full access. How will you audit and reduce permissions safely?

8️⃣ You need to restrict developers from creating IAM users or modifying IAM policies. Which IAM features will you apply?

9️⃣ A Lambda function needs permission to access DynamoDB, S3, and SQS. How will you design least-privilege IAM roles?

🔟 You need to control access to AWS resources based on tags (environment, cost center). How will you use IAM + ABAC?

1️⃣1️⃣ A workload in Account A must read secrets stored in Account B’s Secrets Manager. How will you design this securely?

1️⃣2️⃣ You must rotate IAM access keys for 200 users automatically. How will you implement this?

1️⃣3️⃣ You need to prevent deletion or modification of critical IAM roles. Which IAM guardrails or SCPs will you apply?

1️⃣4️⃣ You must audit all privileged IAM activities (role creation, policy updates, key usage). Which AWS logging services will you enable?

1️⃣5️⃣ Your organization requires a temporary “break-glass” admin role with strict monitoring. How will you implement and control access to it?

